            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path",
      "impact_statement": "The excessive allocation only happens inside ObjectInputStream.readObject of CompactHashMap, CompactHashSet or MapMakerInternalMap. Neither Blaze nor any library on its runtime classpath deserializes Java objects from the network, a database or Kafka. All wire and storage formats are JSON, XML or CBOR. Analysed for Blaze 1.10.0 and 1.11.0, see https://github.com/samply/blaze/issues/4732."
    },
